# Reproducible API + download caches
data/cache/

# Private / enterprise artifacts — SECOND layer only. The primary boundary is
# enforced in code at serialization time (src/boundary.py strips private
# values from public snapshots; export_private_snapshot writes only under
# EROOM_PRIVATE_ROOT, which must be OUTSIDE this repo). These patterns are a
# backstop so a stray private write can't be `git add`-ed by accident. They
# are NOT the boundary — never rely on them alone. See BOUNDARY.md.
data/private/
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.pth
*.bin
*.ckpt
*.npy
*.npz

# Local scratch / out-of-baseline notes
onboarding/

# Per-round audit notes, design docs, inspection snapshots, and the
# automated debug-loop playbook. Local-only — these are the operator's
# working notes rather than published artifacts.
audit/
automate_node_debug.md
NEXT_SESSION.md

# Internal strategy / methodology docs — kept private (the repo is public, but
# the public/private boundary spec, the ML-vs-graph benchmark, the scaling plan,
# the hyperparameter registry, and the trust ledger are operator-internal, not
# published artifacts). NOTE: CLAUDE.md is intentionally KEPT (a generic
# contributor/agent orientation doc); detailed evolving state lives in private
# Claude memory, not in-repo.
BOUNDARY.md
BENCHMARK.md
SCALING.md
HYPERPARAMETERS.md
TRUST_LEDGER.md
# Belt-and-suspenders: the operator's license/moat note is a Claude *memory* file
# that lives OUTSIDE the repo; ignore the name in case a copy ever lands in-tree.
project_license.md
